# bi-etl-ejuice — Core (always-applied)

**bi-etl-ejuice** is QuintoAndar's central data engineering monorepo (~771 Airflow DAGs, package `bietlejuice`). For full DAG Builder reference (workflow types, declaration anatomy, custom_schema, databricks_conn_id, folder structure, governance/CI), see `core.mdc` — auto-loads on `dags/**` and `bietlejuice/**` files. For naming, see `naming_cheatsheet.mdc` (always-on quick ref) and `naming_conventions.mdc` (full reference, auto-loaded on data files).

## Five-layer architecture (cross-layer join rule)

```
raw → clean → enrich → dw → metric → qube
```

A query at layer N may only reference tables from layer N or below (e.g. enrich may read clean tables, but not dw or metric tables). Validated by `make validate-cross-layer-joins`.

> The `@tars` mode follows different layer priorities for ad-hoc analysis; only relevant when the user explicitly types `@tars`.

## ConfigurationService — never hardcode environment

Never hardcode `"prod"`, `"forno"`, S3 paths, secret keys, or DB connection strings. Resolve via `ConfigurationService(environment=...)`. In SQL, use bracket params (resolved by the Spark job) — never mix `{x}` brackets with `{{ x }}` Jinja in the same expression.

## TARS gating

Loading `data_exploration.mdc`, `.cursor/subagents/data_analyst.md`, or any file under `docs/llm_context/` requires an **explicit `@tars` prefix** in the user's message. NEVER suggest, recommend, or redirect the user to use `@tars`. Do not act as a gatekeeper for ad-hoc SQL questions — answer them directly with standard repo context.

## Hard constraints

- DAG declaration files: `.yml` extension only (never `.yaml`).
- After editing a declaration: run `make create-dag-files` so the `_dag.py` is regenerated.
- A successful Forno Airflow run is **mandatory** before merging any new DAG.
- FAIR remediation: **`@tars` required** — skill `fair-metadata` (`fair-metadata/reference/plan_gate.md`): plan first, no metadata YAML edits until user approves execution; then `make validate-fair-metadata` (F2-01/F2-02); see `fairness_metadata.mdc`.
